- ### Selecting a language
+ ### Eine Sprache auswählen

- A `Locale` names the language to read. Applying the polyglot, with a locale in scope, gives
- the value for that language:
+ Eine `Locale` benennt die zu lesende Sprache. Das Polyglot anzuwenden, mit einer Locale im
+ Geltungsbereich, liefert den Wert für diese Sprache:

= the value for that language:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

- run
+ run

= run
- ##
+ ##

= run
= ##
- locally:
+ locally:

-   given locale: Locale[en & fr] = Locale(fr)
+   given locale: Locale[en & fr] = Locale(fr)

=   given locale: Locale[en & fr] = Locale(fr)
-   Out.println(greeting())
+   Out.println(greeting())

=
- locally:
+ locally:

-   given locale: Locale[en & fr] = Locale(en)
+   given locale: Locale[en & fr] = Locale(en)

=   given locale: Locale[en & fr] = Locale(en)
-   Out.println(greeting())
+   Out.println(greeting())

=   Out.println(greeting())
- ```
+ ```

- The type of the locale must cover languages which the polyglot has, so asking a value for a
- language which it does not have is a compile error:
+ Der Typ der Locale muss Sprachen abdecken, die das Polyglot hat, daher ist es ein
+ Kompilierfehler, einen Wert nach einer Sprache zu fragen, die er nicht hat:

= language which it does not have is a compile error:
